# Retire policy 2026-11-20: still in production in 2026 with no announced end; retire dates commented out. Revisit when an end is announced.
# Hyundai i10 third generation five-door, 2020-present.
#
# The AC3 i10: the wider, lower city car with the very wide trapezoid
# grille, the sharp lamps and the blacked-out A-pillar. UK sales from
# 18 January 2020.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyundai_i10
#
# Dimensions 3.675 x 1.680 x 1.483 m, wheelbase 2.425 m (AC3; the Indian AI3
# is a different, longer car and is not represented).
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true side elevation of a red car; the front
# and rear three-quarters show the grille, lamps and tail.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the Hyundai Motor UK launch release of 18 December 2019:
# Polar White, Tomato Red, Phantom Black and Sleek Silver. Weights 12, 10, 10,
# 8, total 40, provisional.
#
# Speed 165 km/h. Comfort 70/435, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 70. Classes 0,1.
# Dates are road presence: 2020 intro, retire dates commented out (still in production in 2026).
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/hyundai-i10-mk3.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/hyundai-i10-mk3.dae. References:
# citycars/references/hyundai-i10-mk3/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: an independent AC3 hull, not a variant of the Mk2.
# Pre-facelift fascia. The overhang split is reconciled to the published
# dimensions. The rear-quarter trim, rear lamp wraps and grille internals are
# simplified.


